 "result": "Based on the subagent's report, these are the failures not directly caused by the `partitioned` `set_cookie` error:\n\n1. **`test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view`**: raises `RuntimeError: Install Tessel with the 'async' extra`, because asgiref isn't installed. This one is a missing dependency, not a Werkzeug issue.\n\n2. **`test_request.py::test_limit_config`**: `request.max_form_memory_size` is `None` instead of 500000. The subagent suspects this is also the old Werkzeug (3.0.3 lacks that newer attribute). That makes it a version mismatch of the same kind, but a different code path from `set_cookie`.\n\n3. **`test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`**: fails with a pytest-level error that the subagent did not diagnose, so its cause is unknown.\n\nOne more is only probably related: `test_reqctx.py::test_session_dynamic_cookie_name` returns an HTML error page instead of `b'value set'`. The subagent guessed this is a side effect of the `set_cookie` error, but did not confirm it.\n\nThe subagent didn't list every one of the 24 failures, only about 20 attributed to the main cause plus these. So I can't name the remaining ones with certainty. If you want, I can have it re-run and list all 24 with their individual causes.",
